joe Linux: naming an anonymous mapping leaves errno as it was. Naming needs a kernel built with
CONFIG_ANON_VMA_NAME, as Android's kernels are and many Linux kernels (Debian's cloud kernels, for
one) are not; there every name is refused with EINVAL, and malloc, atexit, dlopen and new threads
left that in errno when they succeeded. The kernel's kallsyms, which reads errno after getline
returns -1, failed on the empty file its first pass reads. Every name now goes through
__bionic_set_vma_name (platform/bionic/vma_name.h); scudo's and GWP-ASan's are patched in
patches/external/.

